(Regression test: a failed integer cast sets _last_error, but a later
successful integer cast clears it so a subsequent On error does not fire.
The texts are read at run time: a literal that is not a number is refused
by the compiler.)

a text called word is "not a number".
a text called other is "also bad".
a text called digits is "42".
A number called bad is word as a number.
On error print "first".

A number called bad2 is other as a number.
A number called good is digits as a number.
On error print "second".
Print bad.
Print good.
